  "notes": "COMPOUNDS:\n{多|た} (many) + {弁|べん} (speech)\n\nUSAGE:\nCan be neutral or slightly negative depending on context. Unlike お{喋|しゃべ}り, which is casual and often affectionate, {多弁|たべん} is more formal and can imply excessive talking.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {多弁|たべん} (talkative) ↔ {寡黙|かもく} (taciturn)\n- {多弁|たべん} ↔ {無口|むくち} (quiet, untalkative)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {雄弁|ゆうべん} - eloquent\n- {能弁|のうべん} - fluent, articulate\n- {饒舌|じょうぜつ} - garrulous, verbose\n- お{喋|しゃべ}り - chatty (casual)",
